cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "Smith"
    given-names: "Jane"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org"
  - family-names: "Doe"
    given-names: "John"
title: "My Awesome Research Software"
version: "1.0.4"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.1234567"
date-released: "2026-10-03"
url: "https://github.com/username/Reproducible-Research"

Key Fields Explained
• cff-version: The version of the Citation File Format schema you are using (currently 1.2.0 is standard).
• message: A short sentence instructing users to cite your software.
• authors: A list of the creators. You can include orcid links for academic tracking.
• doi: A Digital Object Identifier (commonly generated via archiving tools like Zenodo).
• date-released: The release date of this specific version in YYYY-MM-DD format.

